INT. TRAMPOLINE PARK - PRIVATE PARTY ROOM - DAY

A wall of padded foam. Neon signs: JUMP! SOAR! SURVIVE! A banner reads "SYNERGY OFFSITE 2026." A long table of untouched pizza.

Five employees in matching grippy socks sit in a circle on the floor, cross-legged, as a laminated agenda card makes its way from hand to hand.

HARRISON "HARRY" EZEKWESILI, 40s, VP of Operations, tie still knotted. DOROTHEA PRZYWARA, 30s, the HR manager, clipboard. TREVOR OKONJO-LANE, 20s, an intern with his sock half off. MARGUERITE VOLKOV, 50s, in a cardigan, the longest-tenured. And PAXTON HALE, 30s, from Sales, who has not stopped smiling since he arrived.

DOROTHEA
Okay, everybody, let's share one fear and one trampoline goal.

HARRY
I'll start. My fear is irrelevance.

DOROTHEA
My fear is liability.

TREVOR
My fear is... all of this.

MARGUERITE
My fear is that I'll outlive the company.

PAXTON
I don't have fears. I have opportunities.

A beat. Everyone looks at Paxton.

HARRY
Paxton, that's a fear in disguise.

PAXTON
Is it?

DOROTHEA
It is.

TREVOR
Definitely.

MARGUERITE
I'll allow it.

DOROTHEA
Trampoline goals?

HARRY
Backflip.

DOROTHEA
No injuries.

TREVOR
Escape.

MARGUERITE
A nap.

PAXTON
A synergistic pyramid.

HARRY
Let's jump.

They rise. The trampolines are a field of black. Harry steps on. Bounces once. Bounces twice. His tie flaps over his shoulder.

HARRY
This isn't so bad.

He bounces higher. Dorothea joins. Then Trevor. Then Marguerite, solemn as a monk. Paxton cannonballs onto the biggest trampoline, shouting.

PAXTON
Pyramid!

They stack awkwardly. Harry on the bottom. Dorothea on his shoulders. Trevor on hers. Marguerite on his. Paxton climbs to the top, hands overhead.

PAXTON (CONT'D)
Synergy!

The pyramid sways. Gasps. Dorothea's clipboard slips. Trevor loses a sock. The whole pile topples sideways into the foam pit with a majestic thump.

Silence.

A hand emerges, then a head. It is Marguerite. She spits out foam.

MARGUERITE
That was the best meeting we have ever had.

One by one, the others surface, laughing. Harry pulls off his tie and flings it into the air.

HARRY
Let's do it again.

They scramble. A whistle shrills from the wall speaker.

DOROTHEA
Time!

They sag. Harry sighs.

HARRY
(to Dorothea)
Put that in the minutes.

DOROTHEA
(writing)
"Synergy achieved."

TREVOR
Can I go home now?

MARGUERITE
Not before the pizza.

They move toward the table. Paxton lingers. He looks back at the foam pit, grinning at the wreckage.

PAXTON
(to himself)
Opportunities.
